    "note": "**Portrait fix — the stretched components are corrected. (Rebuild CORE + templates + reload.)**\n\nYou were right: the canvas child was being *stretched* to the landscape panel, not letterboxed. Root cause was in the engine — a nested mosaic child's aspect was inferred only from intrinsic MEDIA, and our canvas is purely procedural (lavfi/text/mask), so it fell back to the parent tile size and stretched.\n\n**Fix (2 parts):** the canvas child now **declares its `size`** (the target-canvas container), and the engine's `inferChildNaturalDims` **honors a declared `size`** — so the parent's `contain` placement **letterboxes** a non-panel-aspect layout instead of stretching it.\n\nI rendered this exact candidate and confirmed on a frame: portrait canvas **centred + letterboxed** in the panel, tiles portrait (540×640), inspector X/W/H = 540/540/640, info bar `canvas 1080×1920 · precision 2×3 · min feasible 2×3 px`. Everything (camera, dividers, cursor, tiles) scales into the container correctly.\n\n*(Core changed — `packages/core` rebuild required. 174 tests green. Default 1920×1080 unaffected.)*\n\nThe letterbox bars currently show the panel/doc background (black here).",
